  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.0: Breaking: customer create no longer has --contact-number, --contact-name, --contact-email or --contact-mobile, and a customer create or update --file with Contacts is rejected with exit code 2 naming customer contact create, because DK Plus ignores contacts in the customer document; the new customer contact list, get, create, update and delete commands manage contacts (create and update take direct options or a CustomerContactCreateRequest or sparse CustomerContactUpdateRequest --file; delete requires --yes; list uses the new customer.contact column profile). Breaking: customer create no longer has --receiver-number, --receiver-name, --receiver-email or --receiver-phone, a customer create or update --file with Receivers is rejected with exit code 2 naming customer receiver create, and one with Memos is rejected as read-only, because DK Plus ignores receivers and memos in the customer document (customer memos have no write endpoint); the new customer receiver list, get, create, update and delete commands manage item receivers (create and update take direct options or a CustomerReceiverCreateRequest or sparse CustomerReceiverUpdateRequest --file; delete requires --yes; list uses the new customer.receiver column profile). customer contact update and customer receiver update --file with a document that sets no member stop with exit code 2 before any request. Breaking: product and memo --file documents use the new nested request types; a nested QuantityInStock, QuantityOnBackOrders, QuantityPoOrders, QuantityOnHand, LastPurchased* or Modified key is rejected with exit code 2 naming the replacement instead of being sent, and ObjectDate is rejected as read-only in product, customer, vendor and work-request files. warehouse update-product --file now reads a ProductWarehouseSettingsRequest instead of the ProductWarehouse read model: stock quantities (including variation Quantity and QuantityOnBackOrders) are rejected naming inventory journal or count, Modified as read-only, and the earlier wire spellings LocationInWarehouse, DefaultPOQuantity, SkipPOSuggestion, Code2 and Description2 naming their replacements, all with exit code 2 before any request; it is an ordinary update and no longer takes --yes (passing --yes is now an unknown option). General-ledger account create and tax-group create --file now read GeneralLedgerAccountCreateRequest and GeneralLedgerTaxGroupCreateRequest instead of the read models: Modified is rejected as read-only, and the tax-group wire spellings Dim1, Dim2, Dim3, Reconciliate and InTaxType are rejected naming Dimension1, Dimension2, Dimension3, Reconcile and InputTaxType, with exit code 2 before any request. Unknown keys inside vendor Approvers, Dimensions, Expenses, Delivery, BankAccount and PaymentBankAccount are now forwarded to DK Plus instead of failing with exit code 2. JSON output includes ObjectDate, and Modified is no longer filled from it. ObjectDate is the dkPlus stored time (Stored Date) and the one DK Plus pages and filters on for those entities, otherwise Modified: the -m/--modified-since, --modified-after and --modified-before help says so, the default tables of customer, product, vendor, sales invoice, order, quote, recurring sale, project journal and work request show an ObjectDate column (customer transaction JSON output now includes ObjectDate too, and customer transaction list pages on it), and the customer, product, vendor and sales-document get tables add a Stored Date row. Numeric vendor transaction enum fields (all but JournalType) show their Swagger names instead of digits. Project work-entry updates no longer send an empty Properties object. Commands that take a page number and -n/--count now fail locally with exit code 2, before any request is sent, when page × count passes the DK Plus limit of 50,000 records per query, with a hint to narrow the query with a modified-after/modified-before window or another filter and start again from page 1. dimension list, project phase list, project task list and project journals continue past 50,000 records by re-anchoring a modified-after window on the entity's paging field (ObjectDate where the DK Plus list response has it, otherwise Modified); project work-request list-for, which has no modification filter, stops with exit code 2 before passing 50,000 records, as does any list whose window cannot advance safely. v0.3.1: fixes reads that failed on 0.3.0 because DK Plus returns enum fields as numbers (customer, product, employee, product category, vendor transaction and v2 project journal reads); numeric enum values now map to their members, and an unrecognized value reads as null with the raw value kept in AdditionalData. Text enum fields read a number as its Swagger spelling, so portable Project.Status and v2 order and quote Status read InProgress instead of digits (likewise employee Status, token Type, request-log ServiceType, customer transaction RecordType, product category Type, project transaction fields, v2 Origin and project journal Status); a numeric vendor-invoice ApprovedStatus now maps to its member, and an unknown company or permission enum value reads as null instead of failing the read. v0.3.0 (breaking): customer get --expand Options is now --expand Settings; customer JSON output is the flat DkPlusCustomer shape with enum member names and no options object; product update takes the item code as a positional argument; project request is now project work-request, whose list --type and --status take enum names; --file documents are the new CreateRequest and UpdateRequest types; every --file reader now fails on stderr with exit code 2 for an unknown key on a type without extension data, and for a key from the previous release, a renamed or read-only key, or an identity key in an update file, naming the replacement; vendor invoice and vendor transaction JSON keys follow the public names (id, dimension1, Unapproved); config columns selections that name a removed column (for example Options.VatExempt) stop with the existing update-or-reset message and the project.request profile is now project.work-request; a vendor invoice attachment without content reports a contract error; ordinary create and update commands still need no --yes. purchase invoice attachment without --output saves under the sanitized last segment of the server-supplied name in the current directory and never writes elsewhere; product --file documents with read-only keys such as Attachments, Changes or RecordId fail with exit code 2 instead of being silently dropped; employee list and get output (including --json) never contain payroll fields; sales order and quote Status, order DeliveryStatus and project Status in --file documents take enum member names. Earlier features remain: self-update, column selection, safe contract-mismatch errors, correlation IDs and the branded help.",
